# hw definition for a fork variant of the AET-H743-Basic-Buzz with bidirectional
# DShot (ESC RPM / telemetry over the signal wire) on outputs 3-10.
#
# BIDIR marks the first channel of each input-capture pair: TIM5 CH1+CH2 (3-4),
# TIM5 CH3+CH4 (5-6), TIM4 CH1+CH2 (7-8), TIM4 CH3+CH4 (9-10). Outputs 1-2 are
# TIM8 complementary (N) channels, which can't capture the ESC's reply, so they
# stay plain DShot/PWM: put the motors on 3-10. Everything else is the Buzz
# variant (tone buzzer on S12, S11 GPIO, LED strip on 13).
#
# Board ID is inherited (AP_HW_AET-H743-Basic, 2024), so the .apj flashes over
# the stock bootloader as a normal firmware update.

include ../AET-H743-Basic-Buzz/hwdef.dat

undef PA0 PA2 PD12 PD14
PA0  TIM5_CH1  TIM5  PWM(3)  GPIO(52) BIDIR
PA2  TIM5_CH3  TIM5  PWM(5)  GPIO(54) BIDIR
PD12 TIM4_CH1  TIM4  PWM(7)  GPIO(56) BIDIR
PD14 TIM4_CH3  TIM4  PWM(9)  GPIO(58) BIDIR
